  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB of length MMM, we define two functions:\n\n\nLet f(B)f(B)f(B) denote its bitwise XOR.\n\nThat is, f(B)=B1⊕B2⊕…⊕BMf(B) = B_1\\oplus B_2\\oplus\\ldots\\oplus B_Mf(B)=B1​⊕B2​⊕…⊕BM​, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\nLet g(B)g(B)g(B) denote the sum of bitwise XORs of all its subarrays.\n\nThat is,\ng(B)=∑i=1M∑j=iMf([Bi,Bi+1,…,Bj])g(B) = \\sum_{i=1}^M \\sum_{j=i}^M f([B_i, B_{i+1}, \\ldots, B_j])g(B)=i=1∑M​j=i∑M​f([Bi​,Bi+1​,…,Bj​])Leo had an array AAA containing NNN non-negative integers.\n\nUnfortunately, he forgot the exact values of this array because of an overload of work.\n\nHowever, he does remember that each element was present in some range: specifically, for each index iii, he knows integers LiL_iLi​ and RiR_iRi​ such that Li≤Ai≤RiL_i \\leq A_i \\leq R_iLi​≤Ai​≤Ri​ was true.",
    "constraints": [
      "Input Format",
      "The first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.",
      "Each test case consists of three lines of input.",
      "The first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of Leo's array.",
      "The second line contains NNN space-separated integers L1,L2,…,LNL_1, L_2, \\ldots, L_NL1​,L2​,…,LN​ — the lower bounds of the array values.",
      "The third line contains NNN space-separated integers R1,R2,…,RNR_1, R_2, \\ldots, R_NR1​,R2​,…,RN​ — the upper bounds of the array values.",
      "Output Format",
      "For each test case, output on a new line the sum of subarray XORs across all possible arrays AAA, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "0≤Li≤Ri≤1090 \\leq L_i \\leq R_i \\leq 10^90≤Li​≤Ri​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 100010001000."
    ],
