      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n3 5 7\n4 6 7\n4\n343 10 7 1\n343 10 7 1",
        "output": "98\n1434",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\nThere are 444 possible arrays: [3,5,7],[4,5,7],[3,6,7],[4,6,7][3, 5, 7], [4, 5, 7], [3, 6, 7], [4, 6, 7][3,5,7],[4,5,7],[3,6,7],[4,6,7].\nLooking at all the subarrays of [3,5,7][3, 5, 7][3,5,7]:\n\n[3][3][3] has a XOR of 333.\n[5][5][5] has a XOR of 555.\n[7][7][7] has a XOR of 777.\n[3,5][3, 5][3,5] has a XOR of 3⊕5=63\\oplus 5 = 63⊕5=6.\n[5,7][5, 7][5,7] has a XOR of 5⊕7=25\\oplus 7 = 25⊕7=2.\n[3,5,7][3, 5, 7][3,5,7] has a XOR of 3⊕5⊕7=13\\oplus 5\\oplus 7 = 13⊕5⊕7=1.\n\nThey sum up to 242424.\nIt can be verified that the other arrays have sum of subarray XORs as 25,24,2525, 24, 2525,24,25, for a total sum of 989898.\nTest case 222:\nThe only possible array is [343,10,7,1][343, 10, 7, 1][343,10,7,1].\nIt can be verified that the sum of its subarray XORs is 143414341434."
